        {
          "path": "_m/9/q/d/5/san-luis-national-wildlife-refuge-wp/wilson-s-snipe-40475803613.jpg",
          "filename": "Wilson's Snipe (40475803613).jpg",
          "caption": "San Luis National Wildlife Refuge, Merced County, California\nExplored 3/22/19, Positions 159 - 207\n\nI only noticed this Wilson's Snipe because a Black-necked Stilt was chasing it. It escaped the BNST and hunkered down in the grass with just a bit of its head showing. I shot a bunch of photos and finally gave up on it moving. We returned in 1 1/2 hours after a drive on the Tule Elk Auto Tour and wondered if it might still be there. It hadn't move at all. It was still hunkered down in the grass with just a bit of its head showing. However, this time it raised its body up a bit, and I was able to get this shot. When we checked the next morning, we half expected it to still be there, but it was finally gone.",
          "alt": "San Luis National Wildlife Refuge, Merced County, California\nExplored 3/22/19, Positions 159 - 207\n\nI only noticed this Wilson's Snipe because a Black-necked Stilt was chasing it. It escaped the BNST and hunkered down in the grass with just a bit of its head showing. I shot a bunch of photos and finally gave up on it moving. We returned in 1 1/2 hours after a drive on the Tule Elk Auto Tour and wondered if it might still be there. It hadn't move at all. It was still hunkered down in the grass with just a bit of its head showing. However, this time it raised its body up a bit, and I was able to get this shot. When we checked the next morning, we half expected it to still be there, but it was finally gone.",
          "width": 4264,
          "height": 2843,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "Becky Matsubara from El Sobrante, California",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wilson%27s_Snipe_(40475803613).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "san-luis-national-wildlife-refuge-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "9qd5",
